20an|n|To form or create; especially, to mold or make into a particular form; to give proper form or figure to. ; To adapt to a purpose; to regulate; to adjust; to direct; as, to shape the course of a vessel. ; To image; to conceive; to body forth. ; To design; to prepare; to plan; to arrange. ; Character or construction of a thing as determining its external appearance; outward aspect; make; figure; form; guise; as, the shape of a tree; the shape of the head; an elegant shape. ; That which has form or figure; a figure; an appearance; a being. ; A model; a pattern; a mold. ; Form of embodiment, as in words; form, as of thought or conception; concrete embodiment or example, as of some quality. ; Dress for disguise; guise. ; A rolled or hammered piece, as a bar, beam, angle iron, etc., having a cross section different from merchant bar. ; A piece which has been roughly forged nearly to the form it will receive when completely forged or fitted.	a:g68,94,3;1u8m,73,6;16o7,73,5;j0a,72,2;ixb,71,3;1qut,70,4;1jrb,55,118;guo,49,2;1jnw,45,4;1x2h,41,5;l27,41,8;4nt,36,4;158d,36,35;2h2g,35,12;2brx,32,4~1jrb,55,118;y7k,20,80;1xvf,20,66;82u,19,38;158d,36,35;lsa,11,31;6kc,22,23;22zk,15,20;2h2g,35,12;x78,9,10;s7r,26,8;1jw6,29,8;l27,41,8;fj7,30,8;h90,9,7	v:10ct,20,3;k2y,19,3;cv7,0,6~cv7,0,6;k2y,19,3;10ct,20,3	V:1gjt,7,5~1gjt,7,5	n:fxq,71,3;286c,59,10;ixb,56,1;j06,56,4;1uj9,47,2;1jrb,44,58;158d,40,46;213s,37,4;dvh,36,3;12kw,33,9;1x3j,31,4;b3p,29,2;2brx,28,3;oc1,26,5;7db,26,14~1jrb,44,58;158d,40,46;7db,26,14;22pu,17,11;286c,59,10;12kw,33,9;197i,13,7;243a,4,6;27ms,24,6;2g38,25,5;oc1,26,5;1mgt,6,4;12wb,2,4;j06,56,4;213s,37,4	N:1l94,113,84;1u6f,59,3;1e9t,59,4;l7q,47,11;x84,32,2;1b5w,22,7;t69,14,3;35u,13,4~1l94,113,84;l7q,47,11;1b5w,22,7;35u,13,4;1e9t,59,4;t69,14,3;1u6f,59,3;x84,32,2
