20ck|n|A sheave. ; A quantity of the stalks and ears of wheat, rye, or other grain, bound together; a bundle of grain or straw. ; Any collection of things bound together; a bundle; specifically, a bundle of arrows sufficient to fill a quiver, or the allowance of each archer, -- usually twenty-four.	N:evg,140,1;28qy,65,1~evg,140,1;28qy,65,1
20ck|v|To gather and bind into a sheaf; to make into sheaves; as, to sheaf wheat. ; To collect and bind cut grain, or the like; to make sheaves.	o:evg,140,1~evg,140,1
