20dk|v|of Shed ; To separate; to divide. ; To part with; to throw off or give forth from one's self; to emit; to diffuse; to cause to emanate or flow; to pour forth or out; to spill; as, the sun sheds light; she shed tears; the clouds shed rain. ; To let fall; to throw off, as a natural covering of hair, feathers, shell; to cast; as, fowls shed their feathers; serpents shed their skins; trees shed leaves. ; To cause to flow off without penetrating; as, a tight roof, or covering of oiled cloth, sheeds water. ; To sprinkle; to intersperse; to cover. ; To divide, as the warp threads, so as to form a shed, or passageway, for the shuttle. ; To fall in drops; to pour. ; To let fall the parts, as seeds or fruit; to throw off a covering or envelope.	o:19wv,96,79~19wv,96,79	s:8br,98,4;42h,65,49;22gx,62,10;22h2,44,26;1ol2,36,9;10cs,23,6~42h,65,49;22h2,44,26;22gx,62,10;1ol2,36,9;10cs,23,6;8br,98,4	d:11ic,59,8;1pom,41,5;1tu6,2,2~11ic,59,8;1pom,41,5;1tu6,2,2
20dk|a|of Shed	j:19wv,43,2~19wv,43,2
