20ez|v|To strip or break off the shell of; to take out of the shell, pod, etc.; as, to shell nuts or pease; to shell oysters. ; To separate the kernels of (an ear of Indian corn, wheat, oats, etc.) from the cob, ear, or husk. ; To throw shells or bombs upon or into; to bombard; as, to shell a town. ; To fall off, as a shell, crust, etc. ; To cast the shell, or exterior covering; to fall out of the pod or husk; as, nuts shell in falling. ; To be disengaged from the ear or husk; as, wheat or rye shells in reaping.	o:2guq,40,1;1eii,38,2;xgu,35,1;12zs,33,1;f8w,31,13;1ovs,29,8;1wpg,18,1;1rw1,12,2;ccw,12,1;28v6,10,1;1aur,9,1;201t,7,1;c24,6,1~f8w,31,13;1ovs,29,8;1eii,38,2;1rw1,12,2;xgu,35,1;ccw,12,1;12zs,33,1;28v6,10,1;1aur,9,1;c24,6,1;1wpg,18,1;201t,7,1;2guq,40,1	s:12o,31,78;2cyg,25,1;2go7,7,6~12o,31,78;2go7,7,6;2cyg,25,1	d:12o,4,12~12o,4,12
